  "note": "Independent re-audit after 26d70dfa0d against RFC 9494 Section 4.2 full text. Single restart: retainPeerFamilies now reads the retain-routes answer (dispatchSourceAnswer, recordEarlierRetained) but sends the same retain-routes and mark-stale commands; with no earlier connection retainedConnections answers the source alone, so onLLGRFamilyExpired and onLLGRComplete still send exactly one purge-stale and one release-routes to that connection. The real-RIB helper newGRWithRealRIB now routes every command through answerHook, so the tagged real-RIB roots (TestRFC9494ZeroRestartTimeRetainsThroughTheLLGRPeriod, TestRFC9494RestartTimeThenLongLivedStaleTime, TestRFC9494DelayedDownPreservesLLSTDeadlines, the four omitted-GR-family roots) exercise the new answer-reading path and still require level-1 then level-2 retention with 1ns boundaries before deletion; negatives TestOnTimerExpired_WithoutLLGR, TestRFC9494BothTimesZeroRetainsNothing and TestLLGROmittedGRFamilyWithoutLLSTIsRemoved still require removal. The RIB change (retainPhysicalStateLocked no longer refuses while an earlier connection owns routes) repairs the consecutive-restart retention, whose own row RFC9494-4.2-7 tags it. The new reconnect revocation in llgrFamilyActive acts only after re-establishment, outside this row's down interval.",
